the los angeles home called the one  which the developer had hoped to sell  for a reported 500 million dollars is  being sold to fashion nova's owner  richard sagian for less than half that  lofty amount the house is being sold for  141 million dollars during a bankruptcy  auction through concierge auctions this  week more than double the previous world  record for a u.s home auction the house  was originally listed at 295 million  dollars developed by nile miami the huge  over 100 000 square foot estate took  more than 10 years to build and created  a huge debt for nyami twice the size of  the white house it is one of the largest  homes built in los angeles it spans over  3.8 acres features an outdoor mode of  water on three sides of the home and a  400 foot outdoor running track the home  is reported to have 21 bedrooms 42 full  bathrooms and seven half bathrooms the  home has five swimming pools including  one impressive indoor pool a full  service hair salon and spa a putting  green a ten thousand bottle wine cellar  tennis court and even a nightclub  it offers a 360 degree view of the city  skyline the san gabriel mountains and  the pacific ocean  the builders development company  crestloid filed for bankruptcy last year  which forced the home to be auctioned as  part of bankruptcy proceedings the sale  needs to be approved by a bankruptcy  court judge which could happen later in  march currently billionaire and hedge  fund tycoon ken griffin's 238 million  dollar new york penthouse in 2019 holds  the record as the most expensive u.s  home ever sold
 

